YAFAP:

After many years of infrequent, erratic play, a recent personal
renaissance of Nethack interest has culminated in my first-ever
ascension!  Many thanks to all of you who post such helpful advice on
RGRN.

My dwarven valkyrie started with a successful run of the protection
racket.  A co-aligned altar in Minetown was good for Mjollnir very
early as a gift from my god, which I quickly rustproofed and used to
great effect.  I also found a BoH very early in the game, just below
minetown as I recall, which was a good thing considering my reward for
Sokoban was the amulet of reflection (not a fan).  Somewhere above
Medusa, an opulent throne was good for a wish: blessed fixed +0 silver
dragon scale mail.  (I had already found a cloak of magic resistance by
then, and prefer to keep my amulet slot open for life-saving, though at
the time I was wearing an amulet of magical breathing for kicks.)  My
reflection made short work of Medusa, and I elected to loot Croesus
blind and buy more protection before going on the Quest.  By the time I
completed the quest and the Castle and had made my wishes (blessed
t-shirt, gauntlets of power, magic marker, speed boots, blessed scrolls
of genocide, etc.), I was feeling fairly invincible.  At this point, I
took the plunge into Gehennom.  Hello/goodbye Vlad.  Hello/goodbye
Rodney.  This was my first-ever game to encounter the Wizard, or to
reach the vibrating square.  I invoked, descended.  A few turns later I
notice Yeenoghu has appeared next to me.  I kill him and see that he
dropped what appeared to be the *real* Amulet.  I couldn't quite
believe this, but used telepathy to verify that the High Priestess was
dead (before I had even laid eyes on her).  No trouble really until the
plane of air, where air elementals made the most significant decrease
in my HP since I completed the quest, but still nothing too scary.
Lucked out on the astral plane, finding the correct altar on the first
try.  I had no conflict, using instead a /oT to clear a path in front
of myself.  The rest, my friends, is history...

foosh, lawful female dwarven Valkyrie




